##############################################################################
# 9. Signals
# Three statements about direction, each in its own frame:
#  - era:appliesToDirection on the net point reference: relative to the linear element (origin to end);
#  - era:hasOrientation: direction and side relative to the carrier linear element;
#  - era:signalOrientation: relative to the direction of the line (rising kilometrage).
# On an element that runs against the line they give different values.
##############################################################################

